# TrueLens environment files live with the two services, not here:
#
#   backend/.env.example    the FastAPI service (port, CORS, limits, artifacts, lifecycle, signing key)
#   frontend/.env.example   the Next.js site (the API origin, batch ceiling)
#
# Copy each one next to its service (`backend/.env`, `frontend/.env.local`). There is no shared root
# environment: the browser calls the API directly, so the two halves are joined by one URL on the
# frontend side and one CORS allowlist entry on the backend side, and a value that exists in only one
# of them is the most common way this app appears broken while both services are healthy.
#
# The one thing with no template value is `OVERLAY_SIGNING_KEY`, required when ENVIRONMENT=prod:
#
#   cd backend && uv run python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
#
# It goes in `.env` locally and in the service's environment when deployed. `.env` is gitignored; a
# key that reaches a public commit has to be rotated, not removed.
